Description: Tor-routed media casting appliance for Raspberry Pi
 PiCast turns a Raspberry Pi into a secure, Tor-routed media casting
 appliance. It supports casting from browsers, VLC, and DLNA/UPnP
 renderers, routing all media traffic through Tor for privacy.
 .
 Features include:
  - Tor SOCKS5 proxy integration with stream isolation
  - GStreamer-based hardware-accelerated playback (DRM/KMS)
  - HTTP API and WebSocket for real-time control
  - DLNA/UPnP MediaRenderer support
  - yt-dlp URL resolution for YouTube and 1000+ sites
  - iptables firewall with default-deny policy
